  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "The function $y=2x^3+bx^2+cx+d$ has $y$-intercept at $(0,7)$, a maximum turning point at $x=-2$ and a minimum turning point at $x=1$. Find the values of $b,c,d$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$b=3$, $c=-12$, $d=7$.",
      "worked": "The $y$-intercept gives $d=7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=6x^2+2bx+c\\\\y'(-2)&=24-4b+c=0\\\\-4b+c&=-24\\qquad(1)\\\\y'(1)&=6+2b+c=0\\\\2b+c&=-6\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting equation (1) from equation (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}6b&=18\\\\b&=3\\\\2(3)+c&=-6\\\\c&=-12.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $b=3$, $c=-12$ and $d=7$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 46
  },
